#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133516 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d7509fa-a254-5b78-b307-3e0c4ef4d9ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With a Lower Bound"}] :question/id #uuid "38b4473a-f956-5af5-863b-387dc10b4924" :question/math-academy-id "e-13362" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n![](images/17/1714eb4797f7b318f5e957db7ab0f322fffb2eb2c9bf03f68e3acc08ec399849.svg)\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x \\geq 0,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n![](images/4f/4f0d336b322f68550c50d65380e26ffb33bdd55beab0c7d429e7b4055f973b57.svg)\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & =-{e}^{-t}{|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}+1 \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n![](images/9e/9e1b63a37177781672b70c3a6c01b1b752164b976b6e9982e07d510d468353aa.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133517 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b0ce833-e045-5aff-94a4-f9ad56cdb904" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a CDF Given a PDF That’s Nonzero Over All Real Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "98dd834c-ac74-5cdd-88ee-060fd9ac689d" :question/math-academy-id "e-13363" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x) = e^{-|2x|}, \\quad x \\in (-\\infty, \\infty),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n![](images/40/40ebced9e322ef969e40733356aacdb3971e14276bc6ad54691aeea21b14c488.svg)\n\nLet's compute the integrals.\n\n- If $x \\leq 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x > 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n![](images/92/9293ff0dab0e6c12fd143ec5f8a9d72edfce74fcddae2397f19d0e82a8b767cc.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133518 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eedcfa3d-b02b-5f96-99f4-cd0a452d272a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With Lower and Upper Bounds"}] :question/id #uuid "4159a407-ea9f-5728-b219-bf1afab732a2" :question/math-academy-id "e-13364" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n![](images/9d/9d755ff833ca8a9134d8f2548b6e7e26221a4814cda8a28093a345a2d321920e.svg)\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0 \\leq x \\leq 12,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n![](images/fd/fd6306e35f5c55b4de635fe7d8967e7783f11c96cee2ea8adfdd17348f97a095.svg)\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{72}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{144}{t}^{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{144}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n![](images/b1/b168cb9b6e4619e7b25cddea9ee671e665d057923b9562ff50d99ce874ea8b90.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133519 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbc399b-90f3-5acd-ac70-7345a8436978" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF"}] :question/id #uuid "707e3b49-9c13-50d8-8a7f-c4d5ec44e0ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-13365" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n![](images/97/9792a5033ccd5f6f8198e3465899c752ddd4ae0986b324c13575c1a92e1ff3c7.svg)\n\nfind $P(2\\leq X \\leq 6).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval. So we can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 6) & =P(2<X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 6)-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =F(6)-F(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{2}-25}{75}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{75}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d7509fa-a254-5b78-b307-3e0c4ef4d9ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With a Lower Bound"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36a08189-b91b-5a20-b7ab-cd5b33daebf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/20}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424121} {:answer/id #uuid "63f468a1-66c1-59cb-86ef-0e77953938a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{{e}^{-x/20}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424127} {:answer/id #uuid "713d0b3e-c9bb-554a-b337-a9f036666fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-20{e}^{-x/20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424129} {:answer/id #uuid "74a5f07c-c3bf-5c2c-a586-05b1a17ea2f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}{e}^{-x/20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424130} {:answer/id #uuid "ad1adf91-dd13-599a-aacf-34ab3e99b819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-x/20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad1adf91-dd13-599a-aacf-34ab3e99b819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-x/20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424135} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d1d5c23-5aca-5a94-9f2b-7f2199c25b68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9bc932a7-b704-59fd-b0c1-c79e29ca1ef0" :question/math-academy-id "q-126151" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20}{e}^{-x/20},\\, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 0,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{20}{e}^{-t/20}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & =-{e}^{-t/20}{|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/20}+1 \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-x/20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ 1-{e}^{-x/20}, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbc399b-90f3-5acd-ac70-7345a8436978" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f9e3f9-5178-5f25-af6a-daa6ab351cf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424116} {:answer/id #uuid "0fbef09a-e8ff-5508-9488-c6c964ed4029" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424117} {:answer/id #uuid "17a75073-455d-5976-ba1c-b3f22347a040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424118} {:answer/id #uuid "3111cc62-9d7f-5a21-8f89-33bb0b009b9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{48}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424120} {:answer/id #uuid "529bbff1-ee9c-5239-b9f3-b7e4f26f33fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fbef09a-e8ff-5508-9488-c6c964ed4029" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424117} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8a9fa39-360a-5d80-8fca-fb43fa89be61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cbafb4bb-6bd6-540c-9367-06ab0b677b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-126178" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{96}({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}-3), & 1\\le x\\le 3 \\\\ 1, & x>3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>2).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-F(2) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{96}({2}^{4}+2(2)^{2}-3) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{21}{96} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d7509fa-a254-5b78-b307-3e0c4ef4d9ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With a Lower Bound"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4d86307-444b-5404-bf96-e83b782452e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4d86307-444b-5404-bf96-e83b782452e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424136} :answer-field/id #uuid "064b270e-fcf7-5b15-ad01-0cc140059469" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "481bd08b-bf47-54b5-b36c-cbccf6d7d5b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-210757" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 1,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{4}{{t}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b0ce833-e045-5aff-94a4-f9ad56cdb904" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a CDF Given a PDF That’s Nonzero Over All Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8dd2c37-ec9c-5602-ab5a-e63c24ab6b8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x}}{1+e^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8dd2c37-ec9c-5602-ab5a-e63c24ab6b8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x}}{1+e^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419908} :answer-field/id #uuid "13407dc0-5b13-5eaa-91b6-bca274b27437" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1bbb59a5-e080-5eb3-8f00-497d7dc7343f" :question/math-academy-id "q-210766" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$\n\n$F(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{{e}^{t}}{(1+{e}^{t})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{t}}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{x}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1+{e}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eedcfa3d-b02b-5f96-99f4-cd0a452d272a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With Lower and Upper Bounds"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9092706e-4579-52cd-b336-558d7e1b9f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419896} {:answer/id #uuid "b909905a-559d-5031-bfb7-8668badafec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}(x+3)}{324}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b909905a-559d-5031-bfb7-8668badafec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}(x+3)}{324}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424137} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbd2268b-230b-5334-ac68-b3b22356482f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dad3449e-8974-53d7-9ad6-1544954b39d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-210788" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{108}x(x+2),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0\\le x\\le 6,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{108}t(t+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{324}{t}^{2}(t+3)|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b0ce833-e045-5aff-94a4-f9ad56cdb904" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a CDF Given a PDF That’s Nonzero Over All Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f0f787d-1687-5d7b-90fc-bcc440b2102f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}-1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419875} {:answer/id #uuid "6178be04-2216-5153-b323-5257d0136d60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419880} {:answer/id #uuid "9506108c-e704-538c-b725-308070b7259a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}}{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419900} {:answer/id #uuid "c702e577-7142-5b26-9822-367c7f969cb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}}{\\pi }-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419913} {:answer/id #uuid "e9553f1f-e879-592c-9f68-96e639709428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6178be04-2216-5153-b323-5257d0136d60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419880} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a631477-d8b0-5499-9e18-4bec118a663c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aa0570cf-0a8d-5b19-8cfc-d1d338d11235" :question/math-academy-id "q-89631" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{\\pi (1+{e}^{2x})},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{\\pi (1+{e}^{2t})}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{t}}{\\pi }|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡{e}^{x}}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eedcfa3d-b02b-5f96-99f4-cd0a452d272a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With Lower and Upper Bounds"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ea5a4d8-cee6-5f5b-9559-0597059ae4e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}-4x+3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424119} {:answer/id #uuid "47fbec0e-7c87-50b2-b20a-31977a9c56d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x+3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424122} {:answer/id #uuid "624998d8-03eb-57ee-930b-8fdefbbf7c6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3-{x}^{2}+4x}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424126} {:answer/id #uuid "8370b066-0576-542b-8883-25e20f54d4ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-2x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424132} {:answer/id #uuid "8deef2d1-1973-51e5-9cbf-ea501d5e8c27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+12x-9}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ea5a4d8-cee6-5f5b-9559-0597059ae4e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}-4x+3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424119} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e5a55d3-f519-5435-8ffd-ee8305a73bcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4087990a-4ed6-57e2-a3df-7711bffc8cc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-89659" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}(x-2),\\, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<3 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $3\\le x\\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<3 \\\\ {\\int }_{3}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{3}^{x}\\frac{2}{3}(t-2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{3}t(t-4)|}_{3}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}x(x-4)+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-4x+3}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<3 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-4x+3}{3}, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbc399b-90f3-5acd-ac70-7345a8436978" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e656111-b56c-58e0-b523-b0edd9650549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424123} {:answer/id #uuid "616c4e05-5002-58ab-b3bb-58e10d3a8092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424125} {:answer/id #uuid "6f86bba4-cf32-5b63-95b2-322fa3b1a857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424128} {:answer/id #uuid "7b06527d-a247-549f-874c-21500db45064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424131} {:answer/id #uuid "99eb6595-a15f-5755-a0e3-76f958a96458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f86bba4-cf32-5b63-95b2-322fa3b1a857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424128} :answer-field/id #uuid "29e83422-0d19-5c35-89b8-d714903a72c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a285feed-066b-52a2-a5c2-8c1c741cc3d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-89738" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ 1-{e}^{-2x}, & x\\ge 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>2).$" :question/worked-solution "We can perform this computation using the complement, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-F(2) \\\\  & =1-(1-{e}^{-4}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
